# Benchmark build artifacts
build/

# The run records are the evidence behind chapter VI and are versioned. The raw
# per-request samples are not: they are hundreds of megabytes and the records already
# carry the percentiles and the environment fingerprint every claim rests on.
results/samples/
*.exe
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib

# Python virtual environment
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node modules
node_modules/

# Logs
*.log
*.txt.tmp

# Generated reports
*.html
charts/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The rig's TLS certificate and its private key. Generated by benchmark/make_cert.py,
# never committed: a private key in a repository is a private key on every machine that
# ever cloned it, and that this one only protects a benchmark is not a distinction a
# secret scanner makes. The key algorithm is recorded with the measurements instead,
# which is the part a reader needs.
certs/
